PN,30205
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785989891
OL,3,CMan accused of killing Scottish aid
OL,4,Cworker in Athens expected back in court
OL,6,FAfter allegedly killing Ms Ross,
OL,7,FAhmadzai is accused of sending a
OL,8,Fseries of messages from her phone to
OL,9,Fher friends and family before
OL,10,Fswitching off the device.
OL,12,FHe is then said to have bought another
OL,13,Fphone and texted her friends in
OL,14,FAthens, including his wife,
OL,15,Fimpersonating an unnamed jihadist
OL,16,Fsaying he had killed the Scot because
OL,17,Fof her religion, Greek newspapers
OL,18,FProto Thema and Ta Nea reported.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30206
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785989891
OL,3,CMan accused of killing Scottish aid
OL,4,Cworker in Athens expected back in court
OL,6,FThe newspapers reported his wife, a US
OL,7,Fcitizen named Alaina Hall, told the
OL,8,Fpolice she suspected her husband's
OL,9,Finvolvement in the killing when she
OL,10,Fwoke up to find he was not in their
OL,11,Fapartment and tracked his phone to
OL,12,Fwhere Ms Ross was staying.
OL,14,FMs Ross is believed to have died a
OL,15,Fnumber of days before she was found,
OL,16,Fduring which time temperatures reached
OL,17,F36C.
OL,19,FThe Hellenic Police, Greece's national
OL,20,Fforce, were able to identify her using
OL,21,Ffingerprints.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30207
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785989891
OL,3,CMan accused of killing Scottish aid
OL,4,Cworker in Athens expected back in court
OL,6,FMs Ross, who is understood to be from
OL,7,FEdinburgh, entered Greece on June 26
OL,8,Fand was initially staying with friends
OL,9,Fin Piraeus, a port area of Athens.
OL,11,FShe is then said to have gone to meet
OL,12,FAmerican friends in another part of
OL,13,Fthe Greek capital, but it is unclear
OL,14,Fif this ever happened.
OL,16,FAuthorities are awaiting the results
OL,17,Fof tissue analysis to determine
OL,18,Fwhether she died from suffocation, as
OL,19,Fsuggested by a preliminary assessment
OL,20,Fby the medical examiner.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30208
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785989891
OL,3,CMan accused of killing Scottish aid
OL,4,Cworker in Athens expected back in court
OL,6,FThe Foreign and Commonwealth Office
OL,7,Fsaid earlier: "Our thoughts are with
OL,8,FElisabeth's family during this
OL,9,Fdifficult time.
OL,11,F"We are providing consular support and
OL,12,Fare in contact with the local
OL,13,Fauthorities."
OL,15,FA Police Scotland spokesperson
OL,16,Fpreviously said: "We are aware of the
OL,17,Fdeath of a Scottish woman in Athens
OL,18,Fand are liaising with authorities in
OL,19,FGreece.
